# An ad hoc factor base for side 1 of F9.poly (f = 4*x^5+1), with only a
# few primes around 2^31 and just below 2^32. All are != 1 mod 5, so that
# f has exactly one root mod p, namely (-1/4)^(1/5). The last four are
# above 2^32: las must discard them.
